\\frac{1}{32}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133518 :question/problem "Verify whether the vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent, and find the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace spanned by the vectors $\\{\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3 \\}$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186133518 :question/worked-solution "First, we verify whether $\\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2, \\mathbf{a}_3$ are linearly independent. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{3}↔R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-3)R_{1} \\\\\n&= R_{3}:=R_{3} + (-4)R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -15\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3}:=R_{3} + (-\\frac{3}{2})R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, the pivot columns correspond to the linearly independent vectors $\\mathbf{a}_1$ and $\\mathbf{a}_2$ that form the basis of our span.\n\nNow, the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace spanned by the linearly independent columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{proj}_{S} \\: \\mathbf{x} = A(A^T\\!A)^{-1}\\!A^T\\,\\mathbf{x}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n$[\\mid \\mid \\mid; a_{1} \\mid a_{2}; \\mid \\mid \\mid]$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nproj_{S}x &= \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot (\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix})^{-1} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}26 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}^{-1} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\frac{1}{14}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 26\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186131769 17592186131770 17592186131771 17592186131772 17592186131773] "immutable_fields" [[17592186131768 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131768 :answer-field/id] [17592186131768 :answer-field/key] [17592186131768 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
